# Firebase

Use `@react-native-firebase/auth` and `@react-native-firebase/firestore` only. Auth UX goes through `AuthContext` when the method already exists.

Paths:

- User profile: `users/{uid}` → `{ nome, createdAt }`
- Tasks: `users/{uid}/tasks/{id}` → `{ title, date, hour, category, recurring, completed, userId, createdAt }`

`date` is `YYYY-MM-DD`. `hour` is `HH:mm`. `category` is one of `trabalho | estudos | saude | lazer | descanso`.

```ts
const user = auth().currentUser;
if (!user) return;
const unsub = firestore()
  .collection('users').doc(user.uid).collection('tasks')
  .onSnapshot(snap => { /* map docs */ });
return () => unsub();
```

Always unsubscribe listeners. Persist session with AsyncStorage key `@devapp`. Do not invent collections (goals, etc.) without confirming with backend. Never put LLM API keys in the app.
